  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I wanted to bring it up due to the limitations of shaders mentioned for the Oculus Quest version of VRChat. It would be a tremendous asset for world creators to be able to use a whitelisted mobile shader to utilize vertex colors for lighting. I'd like to point out to the PSO worlds on this to support my case, specifically Silent's world called Mines 1. It would also be a major factor in keeping the world sizes to a minimum, since lightmaps wouldn't be a factor in bloating up the file size. I really hope you will strongly consider this, as it is a good technique in game design.",
